insert into public.budget_of_work (grade, subject, content_markdown, source_file)
values (
  6,
  'MAPEH',
  $bow$# Grade 6 MAPEH — Budget of Work

MAPEH is graded as two components — Music & Arts, and Physical Education & Health — each with its own quarterly grade that is then averaged. The Music & Arts sequence follows the official Grade 6 curriculum guide table verbatim (themed around Philippine history through Music and Arts). Grade Level Standard for PE & Health: "The learners evaluate complex health practices, movements, and fitness skills in promoting personal, family, community, and societal wellness for active and healthy living." The Health content area per quarter below is confirmed from the official Grade 4-10 Health Content Areas appendix table; the source document itself only carries fully detailed competency tables for Grades 4 and 7, so the specific PE game/skill activities for Grade 6 quarters extend the confirmed Grade 4 target/invasion-game and rhythmic-activity progression and still need verification against a Grade 5/6-specific competency table.

## Term 1: Music & Arts — Development in Music and Arts in the Revolutionary Period (1801-1898); PE & Health — Personal Health
- **Music:** Timbre (instrumental ensembles, vocal styles/techniques) and dynamics (dynamic markings) as heard in sacred and secular vocal/instrumental music of the period; active listening, describing, and performing (singing, moving, playing).
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Relevant theater forms and their subjects/themes/symbolisms from the period, with focus on character and conflict; dance forms and their role in different time periods.
- **Health (confirmed content area — Personal Health):** Evaluating complex personal-health practices; assessing personal fitness using simple tests and setting a personal fitness goal.
- **PE:** Demonstrating refined locomotor and manipulative skills in modified team games, building on the Grade 4 target-game foundation; applying rules and teamwork strategies.

## Term 2: Music & Arts — Development of Philippine Music and Arts in the American Colonial Period (1898-1935); PE & Health — Sexual and Reproductive Health
- **Music:** Rhythm (meter, time signatures, rhythmic dance patterns) and tempo (musical symbols/terms for speed), drawn from Philippine classical, semi-classical, and popular music of the period.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays, focusing on dramatic structure; dance forms of the period and their role.
- **Health (confirmed content area — Sexual and Reproductive Health):** Age-appropriate discussion of puberty and adolescent changes; importance of hygiene during this stage of growth.
- **PE:** Organizing and participating in a small class tournament applying fair-play values, extending the Grade 4 invasion-game foundation.

## Term 3: Music & Arts — Development of Music and Arts during the Commonwealth Period and Japanese Occupation (1935-1946); PE & Health — Disease Prevention and Control
- **Music:** Melody (tonality/mode) and harmony (basic accompaniment), drawn from folk music relevant to the period and region; listening, creating, performing, evaluating.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays with focus on staging and spectacle; dance forms of the period.
- **Health (confirmed content area — Disease Prevention and Control):** Identifying risks of substance abuse (tobacco, alcohol) and strategies to resist peer pressure; recognizing signs of common preventable diseases.
- **PE — Rhythmic Activities and Dances (confirmed content area for Q3):** Dance Exercise, dance movements, and traditional dances, building movement competence.

## Term 4: Music & Arts — "My Filipino Identity" (Contemporary Period); PE & Health — Environmental Health
- **Music:** Texture (monophony, homophony, polyphony, heterophony) and form (free-form, strophic, binary, ternary), in the context of the Philippine contemporary period; composing, performing, reflecting.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Performance practices in Philippine history that present and celebrate Filipino identities, applying elements of drama (character, plot, setting); dance forms focused on communicative function.
- **Health (confirmed content area — Environmental Health):** Practices that safeguard environmental and community health; basic first-aid steps for minor injuries.
- **PE — Rhythmic Activities and Dances (confirmed content area for Q4):** A culminating dance/movement showcase demonstrating fitness, teamwork, and healthy-living habits developed across the year.
- **Year-end project:** Produce a contemporary creative work (Music & Arts) depicting historical/cultural/national identity, using relevant concepts and practices from across the year, alongside a PE/Health showcase — together forming the MAPEH culmination for Key Stage 2.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.$bow$,
